      "start_seconds": 1.17,
      "end_seconds": 4.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.89,
      "end_seconds": 10.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Alright, not at all, please sit. What seems to to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.71,
      "end_seconds": 22.48,
      "duration_seconds": 9.77,
      "text": "actually, I've been needing to go all the time, and I wanted to to get it checked"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.06,
      "end_seconds": 26.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Did it it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.36,
      "end_seconds": 33.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "oh around four weeks... no wait it's more like two weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.07,
      "end_seconds": 38.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Mm, okay. So, how much trouble does it it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.41,
      "end_seconds": 41.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Severe, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.62,
      "end_seconds": 46.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "any vomiting or fever at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.83,
      "end_seconds": 51.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "actually, no, no vomiting or fever"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.23,
      "end_seconds": 57.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "any loin pain or vaginal discharge at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.53,
      "end_seconds": 62.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "no I haven't had any of them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.13,
      "end_seconds": 65.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.95,
      "end_seconds": 68.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Nothing unusual no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.24,
      "end_seconds": 72.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "any regular medication at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.96,
      "end_seconds": 74.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "nothing regular, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.86,
      "end_seconds": 78.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.26,
      "end_seconds": 82.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "just my tonsils removed, as a teenager"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.41,
      "end_seconds": 104.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "let's talk a little about your daily life and habits"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.36,
      "end_seconds": 120.67,
      "duration_seconds": 14.31,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I do a yoga class on Thursdays"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.28,
      "end_seconds": 125.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.6,
      "end_seconds": 131.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Um, no, I've always been fairly healthy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.29,
      "end_seconds": 135.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "may I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.8,
      "end_seconds": 139.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.89,
      "end_seconds": 159.96,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "your tummy is soft with mild tenderness low down and no pain in the loins"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.73,
      "end_seconds": 167.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "that's all I needed to check"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.54,
      "end_seconds": 186.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "Taking everything into account this looks most like a lower urinary tract infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.45,
      "end_seconds": 190.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "well, will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.99,
      "end_seconds": 212.35,
      "duration_seconds": 21.36,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like a lower urinary tract infection, but I'd like to confirm. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've been needing to go all the time for two weeks, severe, and no vaginal discharge or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.03,
      "end_seconds": 213.73,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "exactly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.59,
      "end_seconds": 256.43,
      "duration_seconds": 31.84,
      "text": "I'll request a urine test, it'll help with dysuria. I want a urine culture done, that's for recurrent urinary infection. For this, nitrofurantoin, 100 milligrams, twice a day, for three days. You take it by mouth. That should help with urinary infection. Drink plenty of water and don't hold on when you need to go. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.28,
      "end_seconds": 267.35,
      "duration_seconds": 9.07,
      "text": "If you get fever loin pain or vomiting or you feel really unwell please come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.88,
      "end_seconds": 271.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "I, I know what to watch for."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.77,
      "end_seconds": 283.82,
      "duration_seconds": 11.05,
      "text": "Come back if it isn't better in three days. Tell me what you've taken from all that, so I can fill in any gaps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.46,
      "end_seconds": 296.82,
      "duration_seconds": 12.36,
      "text": "So, I take the nitrofurantoin, 100 milligrams, twice a day and come back if it isn't better in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.49,
      "end_seconds": 303.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.2,
      "end_seconds": 307.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "I think I understand everything. Thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.93,
      "end_seconds": 309.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "look after yourself"
    }
  ]
